:mb-0 text-size-chat" style="--markdown-link-color: currentColor;"><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">18. Conclusion</h2><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto">This project builds a convolutional neural network to classify hand gesture images into the classes available in the dataset (such as paper, rock, and scissors). The workflow includes image loading, preprocessing, data augmentation, model training, validation, and performance evaluation using accuracy, loss, a classification report, and a confusion matrix.</p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><strong class="font-semibold">Limitations:</strong> The model classifies still images from the same classes represented in its training dataset. It is not a real-time webcam gesture recognizer. Performance on new backgrounds, lighting conditions, camera angles, or people may differ from validation performance. A separate held-out test dataset would provide a stronger final evaluation.</p></div></div></details></div></div></div><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 end-0 grid min-h-0 max-w-full min-w-0"></div></div></div></div></div></div></section></div></section></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></aside></div></main></div><div id="DndDescribedBy-0" style="display: none;">
